Then in hopSentences: `if (stage === 5) return stage5Sentences(8, t, from, serverAddress, snapshot);` and stage 6:

```js
if (stage === 6) {
  const dnsAddr = snapshot.dns?.address ?? '10.60';
  const denom = t.totalHops ?? 8;
  if (!t.hosted) return stage5Sentences(denom, t, from, serverAddress, snapshot);
  const dnsTail =
    t.status === 'NX'
      ? [`Hop 3/${denom}: DNS (${dnsAddr}) -> ${from}: NX no record for ${t.host}`]
      : [
          `Hop 3/${denom}: DNS (${dnsAddr}) -> ${from}: ${t.host} is ${t.dnsTarget}`,
          ...stage5Sentences(denom, t, from, serverAddress, snapshot).slice(1),
        ];
  return [
    `Hop 1/${denom}: Browser (${from}) emits "${t.request}"`,
    `Hop 2/${denom}: Browser (${from}) asks DNS (${dnsAddr}) for ${t.host}`,
    ...dnsTail,
  ];
}
```

Wait for NX: hop 3 sentence + nothing else; hop 1 and 2 sentences from above. Order: [emit, ask, nx] ✓.

For hosted success: [emit, ask, answer, ...stage5.slice(1)] — stage5 sentences[0] is the emit (already mine), slice(1) gives hops 2-8 → placed at 4-10 ✓ with denom rewritten ✓.

Byte-identical check for host-less stage-6: stage5Sentences(8, ...) must produce EXACTLY the current stage-5 strings. I'm rewriting the stage-5 branch into the helper — the strings must be copied verbatim, only `/8` → `/${denom}`.

Also note the stage-5 async branch sentences use fixed strings like "WebServer (10.40)" and "10.11" — keep.

Also model.js TOTAL_HOPS = { 1:4, 2:5, 3:6, 4:7, 5:8, 6:10 }.

