Angle for router: 215° puts it lower-left beside the network hub (180°). Hmm, backends at 200/160 on the compute ring (one ring in). Network ring radius 2400; router at 215° → position (-1965, -1376)... let me compute: cos(215°) = -0.819, sin(215°) = -0.574. x = 2400 * -0.819 = -1965, y = 2400 * -0.574 = -1377. That's quite far from the network card at (-2400, 0). "Beside the 10.x hub" — maybe closer angle like 160° (upper-left)? cos160 = -0.940, sin160 = 0.342 → (-2255, 821). Distance from network (-2400, 0) ~ 840px — card width ~500px, so gap ok. Hmm at 200°: (-2255, -821). Backends sit at 200/160 on compute ring 1600: (-1504, -548) — router at network ring 200° (-2255, -821) — far from backends, fine. The DNS card is at (-2800, 0) on ring-dns, browser at (-3200, 0). The browser→dns wire passes through... browser (-3200,0) to dns (-2800,0): fine.

