Now fix stepOneHop, btn-play-request, btn-url-go to use totalHopsFor(snapshot):

```js
function stepOneHop() {
  const snapshot = engine.traceHop({...});
  const totalHops = totalHopsFor(snapshot);
  ...
}

$('btn-play-request')...:
```js
$('btn-play-request').addEventListener('click', () => {
  if (timer) pause();
  const iv = setInterval(() => {
    const snapshot = stepOneHop();
    if (snapshot.trace.hop >= totalHopsFor(snapshot)) clearInterval(iv);
  }, TICK_MS);
});

$('btn-url-go').addEventListener('click', () => {
  if (timer) pause();
  for (let i = 0; i < 12; i += 1) {
    const snapshot = stepOneHop();
    if (snapshot.trace.hop >= totalHopsFor(snapshot)) break;
  }
});
```

Hmm — btn-url-go's loop bound: previously finalHop+1 iterations guaranteed termination. With trace.totalHops the bound can be dynamic; use a while with a safety cap: total hops max is 10, +1 = 11; but after finishing, the NEXT stepOneHop starts a new trace (hop 1) — the check `hop >= totalHopsFor` breaks at the end of a trace ✓. Safety cap 12 covers all stages. But careful: for a trace where a hop returns early (frame null — e.g. drain finds nothing?), hop still advances ✓.

Wait, actually there's a subtlety with `btn-play-request`: interval keeps stepping until `hop >= totalHops`. For stage 6 NX: hop 1, 2, then 3 → 3 >= 3 → clear ✓.

Also `renderStageTopology(currentStage)` is called at boot BEFORE viewport init — stage6 nodes must exist before that (renderStageTopology looks up node-dns with a null guard ✓ I added). But activeHopTarget/render flows also fine. However the comp-tab/node-card listener wiring in panel.js happens at module top-level BEFORE my initStage6Nodes call if I place init at boot section. The boot section runs after listener wiring (the listeners are attached at lines ~112-215, boot at ~237+). So if initStage6Nodes() is called at boot, the `.node-card` forEach and `.comp-tab` forEach already ran → dns/router cards and tabs would have NO click listeners! Must call initStage6Nodes() before the listener wiring. Place it right after the imports/consts? The $ references ($('start-button') etc.) need panel.html elements — those exist (static HTML). initStage6Nodes appends to orrery-world and .comp-tabs — both static ✓. Call it near the top, before the listener blocks. Let me insert after `const totalHopsFor = ...` definition.

